he's the MVP of the National Football  League the reigning MVP of the National  Football League who took care of  business last night on Sunday Night  Football against a fellow former MVP of  the NFL and Aaron Rodgers and the Green  Bay Packers he is of the 200 Falcons  joining us Matt Ryan he back here on the  Rich Eisen show how you doing Matt I'm  doing great thanks for having me on  thank you for thanks for calling in  after such a big Sunday night game what  did you guys see on film against Green  Bay that you thought you could exploit  exploit when you got out on the field  against them on Sunday yeah I think the  biggest thing when we watch the Seattle  game was just that there was a  commitment to stop the run from the  Green Bay defense and playing a lot more  single safety coverage than we had seen  from them last year and you know we felt  like our play-action passing game could  could open some things up for us earlier  in the game it certainly did that we  created some explosives and and also you  know created some run opportunities for  us I thought we ran the ball really well  last night well from just the  perspective of sitting on a couch it  sure looks like you guys picked up where  you last left off last year how do you  read it Matt well you know I think we're  doing some good things for sure you know  the first drive last night for us felt  like we got into a really good rhythm  which kind of you know got the ball  rolling for us in that game specifically  in the first half I do think there's a  lot of things we can clean up we're not  where we need to be yet you know but  it's good to be two games into it with  two wins and still a lot of room for  improvement so then I'd like to run  through some narratives that have been  placed upon the Falcons going into the  season by the national media and  certainly I'm sure you've heard it  locally Matt and I'd like you to go one  by one here if you don't mind starting  with the fact that your old offensive  coordinator is now the coach in San  Francisco and you and Steve Sarkisian  wouldn't have that simpatico  relationship right from Jump Street and  it would affect the offense what do you  say to that well you know I think we're  we're you know getting more comfortable  together for sure you know but we've  done a good job the first two weeks and  I think we'll continue to improve on on  on that front it's never easy when you  have a change at that position at that  coaching spot  it's it's there's just everybody's a  little bit different but Steve's been  easy to work with and you know certainly  done a great job for us the first weeks  well how do you do how do you get on  that page that same page other than just  playing football games well that's the  most important thing I think as we  continue to play games and we're in the  the fire together I think that's how you  really connect but communication I mean  open lines of communication is key  that's something that I've learned  throughout my career is to really  communicate clearly with your  coordinator the things that you're  seeing and then vice versa they need to  to really communicate clearly to you  what their expectation is so is today a  day for that yeah absolutely you know I  think Monday and Tuesday following you  know following a game is critical for  for a quarterback and a coordinator  specifically you know early on working  together I think as you get further into  the relationship there's a better  understanding of each other but early on  that communication is key you know post  game so just getting just a little bit  deeper in the weeds on this do you have  a list of things from last night that  you're gonna go in today and say hey  Steve XYZ ABC yeah as we watch the film  together for sure there'll be things  that that we talked about today of Davis  came up in the second quarter or this  came up in the third quarter what were  you thinking here what here's what I was  thinking here here's where you know you  could help me out with this or here's  where I can help you out with that  those are definitely things that come up  and and as I watched the film first  myself but also you know I usually have  a mental checklist of things that we  need to talk about the day after as you  got one for me from last night give you  any nuggets no gets because chick-fil-a  is not open on a Sunday that is true  that is true and I talked about it  because NFL Network has the Thursday  night game where it's the only night in  that new stadium chick-fil-a will be  open man you go I've gotta get some  Nuggets for me I've got a  come to town for that to happen before  we get to the new stadium I do want to  hit another narrative and that is  anytime there is a moment of adversity  Super Bowl fifty one is gonna crop up in  the mind's eye of everybody in the  organization what do you say to  something about that Matt well you know  I think that narrative is outside the  building for sure that's a question that  we've had to answer and I think we all  have answered you know is there as a any  you know residual effect of that I can  speak for for our locker room and the  guys in our locker room you know we're  not thinking about that you know our  guys are focused on on how good this  27-foot 2017 football team can become  and you know we've answered that and  talked about that and that's honestly  that's that's how we feel you know  that's what we're focused on and so we  understand that we're gonna have to  answer questions about that that's  that's the nature of our business but  inside this building I think we have the  right mindset no I did see on NFL  gameday morning uh my pregame show with  the guys on NFL Network yesterday you  carrying some monster huge log in a  piece that Andrea Kramer did about you  guys working with the Navy SEALs with a  former Navy SEAL in the offseason to get  mentally tough for this exact subject of  conversation that we're having so what  what if what have you guys done Oh about  that yeah I mean that was that was one  of the things Dan had us do during the  off season was was have a group of Navy  SEALs from a company called APG come in  and you know they were guys that we had  worked with before but you know just  from a from a you know a standpoint of  mentally being able to move on to the  next mission or the next opportunity  whatever it may be really there's nobody  better to pick their brains than the  seals and the group of guys that we've  gotten to know the last two years I  think they've really helped our team  with that and you know Karen that log  you know I was always a weak link in our  group I was listen to guys yeah they  were pulling my weight which was nice  but you know it was good it was good for  us and I think it brought our team  probably closer together yeah I mean III  thought to myself I'll be honest I'm  like look I feel I'm a team player and I  understand you know I've got to get  better in my profession every single day  but I'm not lifting a log frame luckily  I was with some offensive linemen and  defensive lines and you have made it a  lot easier for myself Matt Ryan here on  the Rich Eisen show I also noticed that  that Dan Quinn is a clock that instead  of any of the numbers on it it just says  the word now so it's half past now it's  and it's 15 minutes to now is that  another thing that he's done essentially  or to to turn the page or is that clock  always been on the wall man yeah that's  been on the wall since he got here it  makes for you know meeting times what  times things are gonna be a little bit  confusing but you know it's something  that that's his mindset and that's no  different from the first day he stepped  into this building you know he talks  about that all the time the most  important you know day or meeting or  whatever is the one that you're in and  you know it's something that he lives by  and I think it you know it translates  into our team I think a lot of guys have  that mindset so what is it like getting  on the field in a game against somebody  of Aaron Rodgers caliber obviously  you've done it many many times with  other people and I understand that every  game is important but when you step out  on the field and you know that Aaron  Rodgers number 12 at the controls for  the opponent how does that affect the  way you go about your business Matt well  you know that they're always in it  he's he's an unbelievable player and  such a great competitor you know that's  we've gone against each other a number  of times and you know he just makes so  many plays his ability to extend play  scramble and find receivers down the  field is he's as good as anybody ever in  my opinion and you know you just know  going into it that you know regardless  of whatever leads that you have they're  gonna continue to battle and chip away  at and you've got to be sharp for four  quarters and really not give them  anything and that's you know that's  probably good advice for any time you're  playing but certainly when you're going  against a player of his caliber and  obviously you'll be in an interested  observer in Monday Night Football  tonight because  next opponent is the lions how do you do  you a game when you're just watching uh  in real time like the rest of America as  a scout in a way I just enjoy it you  know I'll get to work probably more so  tomorrow on on Detroit and on their  defense but tonight you know I'll just  watch casually it's you know maybe  there's something you could pick up here  there I guess you never really turn that  analytical eye off but for the most part  I'll watch it you know just as a normal  sense well plus you're also tight with  Stafford that I know right you're very  friendly with him and your wives are  friendly absolutely you know he's one of  my you know best friends and a great guy  great competitor you know but it's all  bets off this week well then I know when  that happens and I'm sure it's the same  way for him and then you know he  obviously is the the highest paid  quarterback in the National Football  League right now and you might surpass  that very soon can you just give us an  update on what your contractual  conversations with the Falcons has been  so far Matt yeah I mean there's there's  nothing going on and and you know that's  completely normal for for how we operate  I don't worry about it you know I feel  like you know I take care of my business  on the field and leave the business side  of it to my agents and to the front  office here so you know I think it'll  get done when it needs to get done we've  got plenty of time and you know just I  just got to keep focusing on playing  good football well all you got to do is  just look around the new stadium and  know that the team has the money there  was no shortage of dollar spent on that  stadium Arthur did a great job and I'm  really happy for him you know he  deserves it it's been an incredible you  know ride for me to play for him for as  long as I have and last night to see the  stadium open up and to get a win with  the opener knowing that he has put you  know so much of his life into that  building it was it was really special it  looks incredible on TV I got to tell you  you're gonna love it when you tell NFL  Network to get you down for the Thursday  night dance you can get your Nuggets yes  you're gonna love the stadium it looks  incredible  the way that that roof opens up although  I gotta say this Matt in my end of the  business okay in the television in the  advent of 4k does not help me okay I'm a  man pushing 50 you can wear makeup for a  living 4k doesn't help okay so so I mean  now that when you do a play I mean if  you look up you see it on all these  screens I mean my gosh what do you think  about that Matt you're looking up you  see it everywhere yeah we better get the  nose hair trimmer now or whatever  alright Matt thanks for calling in after  a big win good luck down the line I  already look forward to our next chat  thanks rich appreciate it but that's a  Matt Ryan Falcons quarterback the Rich  Eisen show weekdays at noon eastern on  radio stations across the country and  audience if you like that please  download our app there's lots of fun  things there other than just more of the  videos you just saw you can call us from  the app you can email us from the app  just download it trust me you'll enjoy

